  "accessionCode": "CCX-A-31019",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A stitched hide bladder with a carved bone collar and a wooden stopper on a short leash, used to receive melt from a hauling lodge and to keep it liquid inside the shelter. The seams are sealed with fat and ash and have been resealed so often that the original stitching is visible only at the collar. It stands about half a metre and holds some forty litres, which is what one household expects from one arrival. Recovered abandoned at a moved camp, split along the base, with the collar and stopper still attached and clearly worth keeping.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
